# The round set (web/frames/ + web/rounds.json) IS tracked, even though
# make_rounds.py generates it. Generating it needs the dashcam corpus mounted
# and database access, neither of which CI has, so the committed set is the
# only copy a deploy can reach. Regenerating rewrites ~27 MB of JPEGs, so
# regenerate deliberately rather than as a habit.
#
# A generation in progress is not that set: make_rounds.py builds into .staging
# and moves the previous frames aside, and neither belongs in git or in a deploy.
web/.staging/
web/frames.old/

# Stamped into the deploy by staging.yml / release.yml — which build this is,
# and the changelog to go with it. Generated per deploy, never committed.
web/version.json
web/CHANGELOG.md

__pycache__/
.venv/
.DS_Store
.ruff_cache/
